  "limitations": [
    "The experiment is development-only, with the same six cases repeated three times; no new holdout was read.",
    "Raw semantic-choice agreement does not establish that every constraint was extracted or supported. Missing checks can still yield apparent raw agreement.",
    "A model may omit or misclassify an entity; the validator cannot deterministically recognize every semantic constraint.",
    "Field-only witnesses reject identities available solely in candidate titles, outside supplied excerpts, or through supported aliases.",
    "Only up to three selected records were exercised. A1600-token cap is not demonstrated sufficient for eight-record comparisons.",
    "Literal witness generation added false operational failures. Do not adopt this validator as production-ready.",
    "Any production experiment needs versioned canonical witness/reason schema and raw structured outputs preserved through capture and replay; derived IDs cannot stand in for raw proof."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Do not integrate this literal-witness validator. The raw decisions support further consideration of a simpler structured relevance decision without generated verbatim quotation checks, but no further calls or production edits were performed."
}
